  "tarball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/zen-browser/desktop/tarball/1.23.3b",
  "zipball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/zen-browser/desktop/zipball/1.23.3b",
  "body": "# Zen Stable Release\n\n\n## Security\n- https://www.mozilla.org/security/advisories/mfsa2026-106\n\n## New Features\n- Updated Firefox to 158.0\n- Added a `--space <id|name>` option to the command line interface.\n- Library will now show a 'Open in Folder' option and download speed when hovering over the toolbar icon.\n- Zen now creates more accessible PDFs when saving a page as PDF, and when printing on Linux and macOS. This also fixes a variety of PDF rendering issues, such as missing math symbols.\n\n## Fixes\n- Fixed various animation, urlbar and UI performance issues.\n- Fixed Library media tab requesting onedrive to download all files from cloud. ([#15888](https://github.com/zen-browser/desktop/issues/15888))\n- Fixed unwanted label next to the search icon in urlbar. ([#14856](https://github.com/zen-browser/desktop/issues/14856))\n- Fixed Avahi access so CUPS printers are listed in flatpak sandbox. ([#9651](https://github.com/zen-browser/desktop/issues/9651))\n- Fixed various memory leak issues. ([#15954](https://github.com/zen-browser/desktop/issues/15954))\n- Fixed a crash that could occur while Zen loaded website icons (favicons).\n- Fixed menus such as List all tabs, Settings, etc being hard to read with a Windows High Contrast theme. Menu background and text colors now follow the Background and Text colors chosen for a custom contrast theme in Windows Settings.\n- Other bug fixes and improvements.\n\n## Changes\n- Space routing regex will now match URLs as case-insensitive.\n- Library's widget hover list will now only display recently downloaded files.\n- Zen no longer rounds scroll positions to whole screen pixels. Scrolling is now smoother and more precise, especially on high-resolution displays or when a page is zoomed.\n",
